{"seq":36,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r4-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-live-rr-l3-mu-v04-dev/rr-11-l3-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-retired/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T02:05:21.691Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"4047ae3a48f372ffb8ede744e4c538fe308048113491da1d910a44452a0ba183","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","text":"Hi Hollis, here's what I can find on both:\n\nSalina North Gatehouse Check-In timeout: ticket #4409. The only mention is the Central handoffs note from 2 Jan 2026, written before Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Mon 5 Jan. It says you flagged two open tickets on Pree's dealer account before the handoff. #4409 was a timeout that kept coming back on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard, at Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron during the 06:00 flatbed intake. The other was #4412, a small glitch in the driver SMS prompt when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. I can't find any later update on #4409, so I don't know if it was fixed or is still open.\n\nWest yard Door 2 double-booking: ticket #8841. On 13 Oct in #central-random, Tobias checked the Plains depots on his dealer account to see if the webhook patch had fixed the tractor-bay alerts. He said West yard Door 2 was still double-booking when flatbeds checked in early at the kiosk, and he flagged it on #8841 for support. Nothing has been posted since then.\n\nOne caveat: neither source names Marrow Fieldworks with the ticket. They say \"Pree's dealer account\" (before the handoff) and \"Tobias's dealer account\". I'm assuming both mean Fieldworks, so please check that before it goes in the file. For current status, ask Tobias, or check the tickets in the support queue."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","ts":"1792591200.000130"}}
